     "side": "t",
     "title": "31 bits of count, 1 bit of level",
     "text": "The first words of this beep, in ticks: <b>1,875,003↑ · 1,875,785↓ · 1,878,128↑ · 1,878,910↓ · 1,881,253↑ · 1,882,035↓</b>"
    },
    {
     "from": 33.87,
     "to": 42.25,
     "anchor": [
      "p",
      204166.66666666666,
      -2.1
     ],
     "at": [
      720,
      730
     ],
     "side": "t",
     "style": "warn",
     "title": "Hold-off: 8 µs",
     "text": "A fall is written only once the pin has stayed low that long. Here each low lasts 62.5 µs: every edge is kept."
    },
    {
     "from": 44.849999999999994,
     "to": 51.08,
     "anchor": [
      "p",
      1056937.7990430621,
      -1.5
     ],
     "at": [
      720,
      730
     ],
     "side": "t",
     "title": "Ring of 4096 words",
     "text": "16 kB, read every 1 ms by core 1. This group of 3 beeps: <b>4,806</b> edges."
    }
   ],
   "say": [
    {
     "at": 0.8,
     "text": "The pin now carries a clean logic signal. The I O M C U does not sample it at a fixed rate. It records the moment of every edge."
    },
    {
     "at": 11.18,
     "text": "A state machine of the programmable I O watches the pin and runs a counter beside it: one tick every 26.7 nanoseconds."
    },
    {
     "at": 20.82,
     "text": "At each edge it writes one word: the counter, and the level after the edge. Direct memory access moves the words into a ring of 4096."
    },
    {
     "at": 31.57,
     "text": "A hold-off of 8 microseconds drops lows that are shorter. So a fast carrier arrives as one pulse per burst, and the ring does not flood."
    },
    {
     "at": 42.55,
     "text": "Once a millisecond, the second core takes the new words out of the ring and hands them to the detector."
    }
   ]
